    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0217" n="193" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg193"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Judd.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 75.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-06-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 17, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your despatch of May 28, No. 66, and I thank you for the interesting
                    information it contains.</p>
                <p>The Baron von Gerolt shortly goes on a leave of absence to Berlin. He has been
                    long in the service, and holds a distinguished rank in the diplomatic society of
                    this capital. During all the vicissitudes of our affairs, while he has
                    faithfully advocated and defended the interests of his country, he has at the
                    same time been a firm, frank, and hopeful friend of this government and country.
                    It will be especially agreeable to me if you shall be able to impress upon the
                    government of Prussia a conviction that the Baron is held in the highest esteem
                    and respect, not only by the President, but by the people of the United States. </p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norman B. Judd</hi>, Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.<hi rendition="#italic">,
                            Berlin.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
